course: dictionary
lesson: 3104
title: Eighty, eight tens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Eighty is a number, written as 80. It means eight tens. Count in tens: 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, 80. You have said eight tens, so you have reached eighty.
explain: Eighty can also be made other ways. Four twenties make 80, and eight times ten makes 80. Work out both in your head to check they match.
explain: You meet eighty in real life. The text says «many people seventy, eighty or more» live a long time, so eighty is a big age, but it is still just a number of years. Eighty pages or eighty miles means you have counted eighty of something.
fact: Eighty is written as 80.
fact: 80 = 8 × 10 = 4 × 20.
fact: 80 percent means 80 out of every 100.
fact: In Chinese, «bāshí le!» means eighty!
exercise: «Many people seventy, eighty or more» live a long time. Which number is eighty? | *80 | 18 | 800 | 8
exercise: Eighty is eight tens. How many tens make 80? | 4 | 10 | 20 | *8
exercise: Grandma says «bāshí le!» means eighty. Which sum also makes 80? | *4 × 20 | 8 + 8 | 10 + 20 | 4 × 2
test:
Eighty percent means 80 out of how many? | 8 | 80 | *100 | 800
Count in tens: 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, ___ | 71 | *80 | 90 | 100
exam: Eighty plus twenty equals what? | 110 | *100 | 90 | 60
